  "chapter": {
    "number": 136,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(137)",
          {
            "noteId": 241
          },
          "For David, a Psalm of Jeremias."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat; and wept when we remembered Sion.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "We hung our",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 242
          },
          {
            "text": "harps on the willows in the midst of it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For there they that had taken us captive asked of us the words of a song; and they that had carried us away asked a hymn, saying, Sing us one of the songs of Sion.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How should we sing the Lord's song",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 243
          },
          {
            "text": "in a strange land?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If I forget you, O Jerusalem, let my right hand forget its skill.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "May my tongue cleave to my throat, if I do not remember you; if I do not prefer Jerusalem as the chief of my joy.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Remember, O Lord, the children of Edom in the day of Jerusalem; who said, Rase it,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 244
          },
          {
            "text": "rase it, even to its foundations.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Wretched daughter of Babylon! blessed shall he be who shall reward you as you have rewarded us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed shall he be who shall seize and dash your infants against the rock.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
